    "markdown": "![ACL Logo](https://aclanthology.org/images/acl-logo.svg) ACL Anthology ⟨1⟩\n  * About⟨2⟩\n    * Announcements⟨3⟩\n    * Communication channels⟨4⟩\n    * Related work⟨5⟩\n    * Copyright⟨6⟩\n    * * * *\n    * Credits⟨7⟩\n    * Volunteer⟨8⟩\n    * Development⟨9⟩\n    * Feedback⟨10⟩\n  * Using⟨2⟩\n    * Citing papers⟨11⟩\n    * Links in the Anthology⟨12⟩\n    * Data access⟨13⟩\n    * * * *\n    * All FAQs⟨14⟩\n    * * * *\n    * ###### Details\n    * Anthology identifiers⟨15⟩\n    * Names⟨16⟩\n    * ORCID iDs⟨17⟩\n    * DOIs⟨18⟩\n    * Verified authors⟨19⟩\n  * Contributions⟨2⟩\n    * Submissions⟨20⟩\n    * Corrections⟨21⟩\n    * Author pages⟨22⟩\n    * Attachments⟨23⟩\n  * GitHub⟨24⟩\n\n\n## Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts⟨25⟩\nAgata Savary⟨26⟩, Yue Zhang⟨27⟩\n##### Correct Metadata for \nUse this form to create a GitHub issue with structured data describing the correction. You will need a GitHub account. Once you create that issue, the correction will be reviewed by a staff member.\n⚠️ Mobile Users: Submitting this form to create a new issue will only work with github.com, not the GitHub Mobile app.\n**Important** : The Anthology treat PDFs as authoritative. Please use this form only to correct data that is out of line with the PDF. See our corrections guidelines⟨21⟩ if you need to change the PDF.\nTitle Adjust the title. Retain tags such as <fixed-case>.\nAuthors Adjust author names and order to match the PDF.Add Author\nAbstract Correct abstract if needed. Retain XML formatting tags such as <tex-math>. You may use <b>...</b> for **bold** , <i>...</i> for _italic_ , <u>...</u> for _underline_ , <sc>...</sc> for small-caps, <tt>...<tt> for `typewriter text`, <url>...</url> for URLs, <a href=...> for hyperlinks, and <par/> for paragraph breaks.\nVerification against PDF Ensure that the new title/authors match the snapshot below. (If there is no snapshot or it is too small, consult the PDF⟨2⟩.)\n![](https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-tutorials.0/)⟨2⟩\nAuthors concatenated from the text boxes above:\nALL author names match the snapshot above—including middle initials, hyphens, and accents.\nCreate GitHub issue for staff review\n* * * \n\nAnthology ID:\n    2020.acl-tutorials.0 \n\nVolume:\n    Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts⟨28⟩ \n\nMonth:\n    July \n\nYear:\n    2020 \n\nAddress:\n    Online \n\nVenue:\n    ACL⟨29⟩ \n\nSIG:\n\n\nPublisher:\n    Association for Computational Linguistics \n\nNote:\n\n\nPages:\n\n\nLanguage:\n\n\nURL:\n    <https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-tutorials.0/> \n\nDOI:\n\n\nBibkey:\n    acl-2020-association-linguistics-tutorial \n\nCite (ACL):\n    Agata Savary and Yue Zhang. 2020. _Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts⟨30⟩_. Association for Computational Linguistics, Online. \n\nCite (Informal):\n    Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts⟨30⟩ (Savary & Zhang, ACL 2020) \n\nCopy Citation:\n     BibTeX Markdown MODS XML Endnote More options… \n\nPDF:\n    <https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-tutorials.0.pdf>\nPDF ⟨25⟩Cite ⟨2⟩Search ⟨31⟩ Fix data⟨2⟩\n* * *\n##### Export citation\n  * BibTeX⟨32⟩\n  * MODS XML⟨33⟩\n  * Endnote⟨34⟩\n  * Preformatted⟨35⟩\n\n\n\n```\n@proceedings{acl-2020-association-linguistics-tutorial,\n    title = \"Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts\",\n    editor = \"Savary, Agata  and\n      Zhang, Yue\",\n    month = jul,\n    year = \"2020\",\n    address = \"Online\",\n    publisher = \"Association for Computational Linguistics\",\n    url = \"https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-tutorials.0/\"\n}\n```\n\nDownload as File Copy to Clipboard\n\n```\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<modsCollection xmlns=\"http://www.loc.gov/mods/v3\">\n<mods ID=\"acl-2020-association-linguistics-tutorial\">\n    <titleInfo>\n        <title>Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts</title>\n    </titleInfo>\n    <name type=\"personal\">\n        <namePart type=\"given\">Agata</namePart>\n        <namePart type=\"family\">Savary</namePart>\n        <role>\n            <roleTerm authority=\"marcrelator\" type=\"text\">editor</roleTerm>\n        </role>\n    </name>\n    <name type=\"personal\">\n        <namePart type=\"given\">Yue</namePart>\n        <namePart type=\"family\">Zhang</namePart>\n        <role>\n            <roleTerm authority=\"marcrelator\" type=\"text\">editor</roleTerm>\n        </role>\n    </name>\n    <originInfo>\n        <dateIssued>2020-07</dateIssued>\n        <publisher>Association for Computational Linguistics</publisher>\n        <place>\n            <placeTerm type=\"text\">Online</placeTerm>\n        </place>\n    </originInfo>\n    <typeOfResource>text</typeOfResource>\n    <genre authority=\"marcgt\">conference publication</genre>\n    <identifier type=\"citekey\">acl-2020-association-linguistics-tutorial</identifier>\n    <location>\n        <url>https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-tutorials.0/</url>\n    </location>\n</mods>\n</modsCollection>\n\n```\n\nDownload as File Copy to Clipboard\n\n```\n%0 Conference Proceedings\n%T Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts\n%E Savary, Agata\n%E Zhang, Yue\n%D 2020\n%8 July\n%I Association for Computational Linguistics\n%C Online\n%F acl-2020-association-linguistics-tutorial\n%U https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-tutorials.0/\n```\n\nDownload as File Copy to Clipboard\n##### Markdown (Informal)\nProceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts⟨30⟩ (Savary & Zhang, ACL 2020)\n  * Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts⟨30⟩ (Savary & Zhang, ACL 2020)\n\n\n##### ACL\n  * Agata Savary and Yue Zhang. 2020. _Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstracts⟨30⟩_. Association for Computational Linguistics, Online.\n\n\nCopy Markdown to Clipboard Copy ACL to Clipboard\n![Creative Commons License](https://i.creativecommons.org/l/by/4.0/88x31.png)⟨36⟩ ACL materials are Copyright © 1963–2026 ACL; other materials are copyrighted by their respective copyright holders. Materials prior to 2016 here are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 International License⟨37⟩. Permission is granted to make copies for the purposes of teaching and research. Materials published in or after 2016 are licensed on a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License⟨38⟩.\nThe ACL Anthology is managed and built by the ACL Anthology team⟨7⟩ of volunteers.\n_Site last built on 22 July 2026 at 14:46 UTC withcommit 280e4ed⟨39⟩._\n",
